Paseo
https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo
Copyright (c) 2025-present Mohamed Boudra
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Portions of Crusteo are derived from Paseo: the conversation (agent timeline)
reducer in crates/fleet/src/timeline.rs, the tool-call display rules in
crates/fleet/src/display.rs, and the understanding of the daemon wire protocol
documented in docs/protocol/ and implemented in crates/paseo-client. These
were ported from Paseo's TypeScript sources to Rust and modified.

The Burrow daemon in crates/burrow-* implements the Paseo daemon wire
protocol (version 1): message names, envelope, handshake, subscription,
directory-sync and timeline semantics, error codes and reply-naming rules,
learned from Paseo's packages/protocol and packages/server and reimplemented
in Rust. The timeline paging in crates/burrow-daemon/src/timeline.rs follows
Paseo's selectProjectedTimelinePage. docs/burrow/ summarizes the protocol.
The agent tools' catalogue in crates/burrow-daemon/src/mcp/paseo-tools-*.json
(tool names, titles, descriptions and input schemas) is Paseo 0.14.0's own
tools/list output, included unmodified; the handlers that serve it are
reimplemented in Rust, as are Paseo's schedules and push notifications.
Burrow is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Paseo project either.

